<title>USA: Hillsborough County, Fla., rejects utility tax.</title>
<headline>Hillsborough County, Fla., rejects utility tax.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPA, Fla. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida's Hillsborough County Commission has rejected a new tax on energy and telephone services.</p>
<p>The proposal failed in a 4-3 vote Tuesday. It would have imposed a 10 percent tax on electricity and natural gas and a 7 percent tax on telephone bills in unincorporated parts of the county, raising $25.4 million in fiscal 1998 and $38.9 million in 1999.</p>
<p>Tampa Electric Co, a unit of TECO Energy Inc, lobbied heavily against the tax.</p>
<p>Without the new revenue, the county will be forced to make budget cuts beginning in fiscal 1998. Public hearings on the proposed cuts begin Wednesday night.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
